 "id": "T09-b40_shoulder34",
 "title": "Closure gap \u2014 first-contact angle of the jaw before calibration",
 "mode": "linear",
 "units": "deg (servo jaw angle at first pad contact, theta = 0 means rigid contact faces 1.0 apart)",
 "requirement": "The uncalibrated first-contact angle falls inside the firmware calibration window (CAL_C0 -4 .. +4 deg), so CALIBRATE finds it instead of raising a SENSOR fault. T09T (close time, R19) and T09F / T09P / T09H (pad force, R15 and R14) build on this angle.",
 "notes": "The rigid contact faces (PLA nail on A, FSR stack on B) are contact_gap apart at theta = 0. Each finger closes the gap at r_c per radian (r_c is the moment arm of the pad normal), so contact comes at theta_c = -gap / (2 r_c), converted to degrees (-0.441 deg per mm of gap). Angle terms enter directly: the horn trim set by eye at bench step 1, servo repeatability, the dog coupling lash (A lags the horn while closing, so the servo turns dog_lash further) and finger B's backlash lag (the servo turns half of it further).",
 "spec": {
  "lsl": -4.0,
  "usl": 4.0
 },
